# Mapped language diagnostics

This controller owns a separate Problems collection and synchronizes virtual documents
without filesystem access. The enabled caller owns resource settings, edit debounce
and invalidation; disabling diagnostics must invalidate its session immediately.

An identical snapshot updates freshness without clearing problems or cancelling pulls.
Source invalidation clears visible problems and aborts work, but keeps bounded raw
reports per client, URI and wire version. After sync, matching reports are remapped
to the new source snapshot, including prose-only line shifts; changed wire versions
are discarded. Listeners attach before sync; only versioned pushes can be staged.
Unversioned pushes are best effort: LSP cannot distinguish a late old report from a
current report without a version. They are accepted only while fresh and idle, and
cached with the current wire version at receipt, never reused across versions.

Caches keep sanitized ranges and metadata, not server data or source snapshots.
Limits are 16 clients, 64 reports per client, 1000 items per report, and 5000 items
or 4 MiB of serialized items per client. Oldest reports are evicted; oversized
reports are not cached. Client stop (including configuration disposal) purges its
cache even after source invalidation; controller disposal purges all caches.

Pull-capable servers take precedence. Requests omit previous result IDs and accept
full reports only; unchanged reports and relatedDocuments are ignored. Refreshes
coalesce into one sequential, at-most-64-document cycle with no polling or retries.

Only synchronized generated outputs with matching content are owned. Mapping splits
code spans, deduplicates expansions, and never invents locations for wrapper text.
Messages and metadata are bounded; commands, code-description URLs and related
information are not copied, even though relatedInformation support is advertised. Reports retain their independent ownership so clearing
one output or stopping one session does not erase another session’s problems.


```ts : <<diagnostics part 1>>=
import * as vscode from 'vscode';
import * as path from 'node:path';
import type { LanguageClient, LanguageDocument } from './language-client';
import { LanguageLocationContext, mapLanguageDiagnosticRange } from './language-navigation';

type RecordValue = Record<string, unknown>;
const record = (value: unknown): value is RecordValue =>
    value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);
type Problem = { uri: vscode.Uri; diagnostic: vscode.Diagnostic; id: string };
interface RawReport { version: number; items: RecordValue[]; bytes: number; }
interface ClientCache { reports: Map<string, RawReport>; unsubscribe: () => void; }
interface Session {
    client: LanguageClient;
    context: LanguageLocationContext;
    documents: LanguageDocument[];
    fresh: () => boolean;
    versions: Map<string, number | undefined>;
    staged: Map<string, RecordValue>;
    reports: Map<string, Problem[]>;
    unsubscribe: (() => void)[];
    abort: AbortController;
    syncing: boolean;
    pulling: boolean;
}
```

